		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=1345#p1345"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>- Is moment of inertia properly calculated for convex polyhedra?<br><br>It is approximated, convex polyhedra, cylinders and cones are currently using an approximation of the local bounding box for inertia. </div></blockquote>Ah, that's why the spinning top looks kind of wierd.<br><br>You know about this, right? Free code for moment of inertia of a polyhedron.<br><a href="http://www.cs.berkeley.edu/~jfc/mirtich/massProps.html" class="postlink">http://www.cs.berkeley.edu/~jfc/mirtich/massProps.html</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=244">John Nagle</a> — Wed Jul 19, 2006 5:54 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
