		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=1335#p1335"><![CDATA[
The reference says that no object should be bigger than 50 units, so I reduced the big static convex to 45 x 45 x 1.  With that, the objects stabilized properly. <br><br>Now, on to the harder cases.<br><br>(I understand you're trying to do this in single precision. Unless you really need to be on the PS2, don't do that. You spend forever fighting scaling issues like this and explaining why it doesn't work.  And you get wierd problems like physics working differently far from the origin.)<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=244">John Nagle</a> — Mon Jul 17, 2006 7:13 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
